F. PROPOSITION 7.2 -- the offset, by the PAPER'S OWN method
====================================================================================================
  offset = <log10( mu(x_A)/mu(x_B) )>_t with x_B = sqrt(<a^2>)/a0, the paper's own S3.
   k = apo/peri       x_B   v2 alpha=1   v3 alpha=2
          20.51    3.5771      -0.0883      -0.0766
           8.29    2.4944      -0.0624      -0.0602
           3.75    1.8148      -0.0344      -0.0369
           2.15    1.4325      -0.0147      -0.0169
           1.36    1.1628      -0.0029      -0.0035
           1.04    1.0202      -0.0001      -0.0001
  [OK] the v2 published -0.037 dex is REPRODUCED (-0.0344) by this replication of the paper's own method, validating it before the kernel is swapped
  [OK] under v3 the same orbit gives -0.0369 dex against v2's -0.0344 -- essentially UNCHANGED, and still NEGATIVE, so Prop 7.2's sign claim ('offset below the rotation relation') and its detectability problem both carry over intact

